wn `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/` — with the spec, the corpus, and the branch. After each return it checks that every path the adapter touched matches a spec claim, then runs the criteria against the tree, the tests `[tests].select` and `[tests].run` name for the touched paths, and — when the manifest declares `[checks].command` — the tenant's own whole-tree check, from the tenant root. `pass` requires every criterion, the test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; a non-zero exit anywhere iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed budget. `[checks]` is optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused, unlike `[tests]`. A `question` from the adapter halts the loop at once (exit 3); nothing answers it in Phase 2. Every run writes the next `build-NN.json`, with the adapter's transcript beside it as `build-NN.log`. Nothing dispatches build; it is typed by the operator. The full contract is in the Phase 2 issue.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `bin/attavo` — the command: `doctor`, `spec-gate`, `approve`, `approval-status`, `build`.\n- `schema/manifest.schema.json` — the shape of a tenant's `attavo.toml`.\n- `schema/records/` — the shape of each stage's record.\n- `adapters/` — the adapter contract (`adapters/README.md`) and two adapters: `claude-code` and `fixture`.\n- `action.yml` — pins Attavo at a tag and puts `attavo` on `PATH`.\n- `templates/workflows/` — three workflows a tenant copies into its own repository (spec-gate, approve, coherence); nothing here is vendored or run by this one. The coherence job mints and signs the attestation on the merge group, against the commit that lands — no attestation record is ever written to the tree; the signed statement lives in the forge's attestation store.\n- `tests/` — the doctor's proofs and the spec and build contracts' rejection tests, with their fixtures under `tests/fixtures/`.\n\nThis repository contains no tenant name, path, or command string.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
